    {
      "type": "text",
      "gap": 32,
      "role": "title",
      "text": "When the river\nfinds its way home"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "gap": 24,
      "role": "dek",
      "text": "A restored floodplain is teaching one small town to make room for the water."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "gap": 20,
      "role": "caption",
      "text": "Words by Mira Ellis   ·   Photography by Luca Morgan   ·   8 minute read"
    },
    {
      "type": "spacer",
      "gap": 0,
      "height": 18
    },
    {
      "type": "columns",
      "gap": 40,
      "columns": [
        {
          "width": 2.25,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "gap": 20,
              "role": "body",
              "text": "At first, the change was almost invisible. A line of willow cuttings followed an old bend in the river, and the fence that had divided the meadow for a century was gone."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "gap": 20,
              "role": "body",
              "text": "By spring, shallow pools had gathered in the hollows. Herons stood among the reeds. On the path above the water, neighbours stopped to compare what they had seen that morning."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "gap": 20,
              "role": "body",
              "text": "The project began with a simple question: what would happen if the valley could hold rain again? Its answer is neither a monument nor a machine. It is a landscape learning to move."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "width": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "panel",
              "gap": 20,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "gap": 20,
                  "role": "heading",
                  "text": "Room for water"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "gap": 20,
                  "role": "caption",
                  "text": "34 hectares of floodplain reconnected\n\n2.8 kilometres of public paths\n\n16 native plant species returning"
                }
              ],
              "background": "#e5e9df",
              "padding": 20
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "gap": 20,
              "role": "caption",
              "text": "This is a faithful editorial sample with fictional reporting. Inspect the reading rhythm, hierarchy and relationship between the two type families."
            }
          ]
